# Why this Module ships no seed/ directory.
# A marker with no justification is a silent skip in file form; lint-config
# refuses an empty one.

Grafana has conf/provisioning/ and dashboards/, and neither is seed data.
conf/provisioning/ is configuration read at startup — datasources and the
dashboard provider — and is bind-mounted read-only, so Grafana never writes to
it and re-reads it on every restart. dashboards/ ships the provisioned dashboard
JSON this stack opens on, and it is the same kind of thing: bind-mounted
read-only, re-read on every start and re-scanned every 30 seconds while Grafana
runs, so the file on disk is always what Grafana shows. Seed data is copied once
into a volume and then owned by the service, which is exactly what must not
happen here — a dashboard living in grafana-data would survive `pixi run down`
only because the volume did, and would drift from the tracked file with nothing
to say so.
